I was really trying for weaponless, but I had a pick-axe accident.
Even after I lost weaponless, I still never intentionally hit with a
wielded weapon.  I was also shieldless and body-armorless, though I
kept a shield of reflection in my BoH in case I needed to wear an
amulet of life saving.  The vegetarian conduct got lost really quickly,
since I ate a floating eye corpse.  I was too busy thinking "this is
important to eat" to remember it is not a vegetarian food.  When I got
half-way through Gehennom, I started intentionally eating corpses
because I didn't feel like backtracking up to Fort Ludious to get more
food.  I lost the polyself conduct to a polymorph trap, though I was
able to keep the poly-objectless conduct.  I'm really horrible at
conducts.


The Monk was very much easier to ascend than the Tourist.  I ascended
with Monk #3.  I had alot of Tourists that had a YASD in the Gnomish
Mines...

Monk #1 (Chaotic) died very early (Either DL2 or DL3).  I was reading
spellbooks in a shop, and one of the spellbooks teleported me across
the level while I was carrying unpayed items.  The pet died while I was
still trying to get back to it.  The pet probably got killed by the
Kops.  I suicided into the shopkeeper, since I was too lazy to b/u/c
identify the armors in the Gnomish Mines without a pet.

Monk #2 (Chaotic) started with a spellbook of Sleep.  He easily got to
the castle.  Then he got overconfident and tried to melee a Minotaur on
the castle level.  He really didn't have to melee the Minotaur, but
everything else was dying so fast he thought he could do it.  He found
out that Minotaurs can take a XL14 level Monk from full life to 0HP in
one turn.  Monk #2 had problems with his god, since he was able to
sucessfully pray only once before he angered his god by praying after
eating meat.  So this Monk ate alot of meat, and it turned out that
none of the altars generated in the game were at a deep enough level to
generate monsters that can mollify a chaotic god.  It appears that
sacrificing humans does not mollify a Chaotic god, even though it
appears that "appeasement.txt" says it does.  I was thinking about
trying to levelport corpses from the Castle level to the altar level,
but I died so I didn't get to see how well that works.  The moral of
Monk #2 is I shouldn't be Chaotic when playing a character with a code
of conduct.

Monk #3 (Neutral) started with a spellbook of Protection.  It turns out
that lacking infravision wasn't a problem since I got the warning
instrinic at the Minetown level.  Warning is alot better than
infravision, since it can see dangerous mindless creatures (i.e. air
elementals), and it can see dangerous monsters that hide behind
corners.  Whenever warning shows alot of monsters, I mashed the
Protection spell and easily cleared out all the monsters.

Protection was the only spell the monk learned.  My Int stat was 8, so
I didn't bother with finding spells.  I #enhanced marital arts up to
Grand Master, then I #enhanced clerical up to skilled.  I was hoping
this would lower my failure rate on the Protection spell, but it
didn't.  My failure rate for Protection was still around 22%.

Even though this Monk could safely pray, he avoided #offering corpses
because he was afraid that he might get an artifact gift.  He was
thinking that he has to make it all the way to the Castle without
finding any artifiacts, so that he could wish for the Orb of Fate and
the PYEC.  The Orb of Fate allowed the Monk to stay alive, and the PYEC
allowed the Monk to keep the poly-objectless conduct.

My AC ended up being -20.  I could have easily gotten it higher if I
had done my magical object polypiling thing, but I was feeling too lazy
to collect all the magical items from the entire dungeon.

The Monk was easy until I reached the Quest Nemesis.  There was alot of
monsters on the Nemesis level, so I had the Nemesis follow me upstairs.
 Then I danced around the upstairs square until I was able to finally
stand on it.  I had to quaff a potion of full healing, since the
Nemesis does alot of damage.  The Nemesis died fairly easily, though I
already had my full ascension kit.

When I reached the Sanctum, I found out that end-game Monk damage isn't
as high as end-game Tourist damage.  So I put on a ring of conflict.  I
also ended up needing to use some teleport/death/digging wand charges.
I still got through the Sanctum fairly easily.

On the Plane of air, I had to use more teleport/death wand charges,
since it turns out that martial art damage doesn't kill Air Elementals
fast enough.

The Plane of water took a really long time.  Some monster decided to
die on the portal square,  and it took a while before I figured out
what had happened.

I forgot to take off my ring on conflict before reaching the Astral
plane, so I had to teleport the hostile Angels.  I decided to keep
wearing the ring of conflict.  The 2 non-Death altars weren't Neutral.
This is the first time that have needed to deal with the Death Rider.
Death was standing behind the door to the Death Rider section.  I
unlocked the door to the Death Rider section, stepped back a square to
move away from Death, and Death decided to stand in front of the open
doorway.  One of the other Riders was coming really close to me too.
So I threw my last 2 paralysis potions at both the riders, closed the
door, smashed the door with a wand of digging, and snuck behind Death.

Then I got to the Death altar, and #offered the amulet.

